        "id": "ch11_6-1",
        "text": "Provisioning VMs using cloud-init\nWhen you\u2019re dealing with only one VM, things can be relatively simple. But when we have to create\nhundreds of VMs, manual creation can be daunting. One useful tool you can use for such a task is\ncloud-init . Another tool that is suitable for this kind of task is Ansible (there\u2019s more on Ansible in\nChapter 17 ). In this section, we will cover only cloud-init. It was developed by Canonical to be used\nas a tool for configuring VM instances on cloud platforms, and it is written in Python. Currently, it is\nconsidered an industry standard for provisioning cloud images. In the next subsection, we will briefly\nexplain to you how cloud-init works.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Understanding how cloud-init works\n\u2022 Installing and configuring cloud-init\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
